## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to blend topological ordering with DP to compute the longest-path in a weighted DAG and count the number of critical paths, including multiple sources and modulo arithmetic.

## Key Concepts
- Longest-path in DAG with node durations and edge setup weights
- Topological sort (Kahn) to process in dependency order
- DP for counting number of longest paths with modulo

## Code Example
```javascript
function countCriticalPaths(N, edges, dur) {
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  const incoming = Array.from({length: N}, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(N).fill(0);

  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) {
    incoming[v].push([u, w]);
    indeg[v]++;
  }

  const EFT = dur.slice();
  const count = Array(N).fill(0);
  const q = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    if (indeg[i] === 0) {
      count[i] = 1;
      q.push(i);
    }
  }

  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    for (const [v, w] of incoming[u]) {
      const newEFT = EFT[u] + w + dur[v];
      if (newEFT > EFT[v]) {
        EFT[v] = newEFT;
        count[v] = count[u];
      } else if (newEFT === EFT[v]) {
        count[v] = (count[v] + count[u]) % MOD;
      }
      indeg[u]--;
      if (indeg[u] === 0) q.push(u);
    }
  }

  let maxEFT = 0, totalCritical = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    if (EFT[i] > maxEFT) {
      maxEFT = EFT[i];
      totalCritical = count[i];
    } else if (EFT[i] === maxEFT) {
      totalCritical = (totalCritical + count[i]) % MOD;
    }
  }
  return { EFT, maxEFT, criticalPaths: totalCritical };
}
```

## Complexity
- Time: O(N + M) for topological sort and DP
- Space: O(N + M) for adjacency and arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a practical, augmented Trie approach blending prefix queries with order-statistics, a gap in typical BST/trie questions.

## Key Concepts
- Trie augmentation with endCount and subCount
- Duplicates handled via endCount
- Lexicographic kthWord via endCount before children

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.end = 0;
    this.sub = 0;
  }
}
class Trie {
  constructor(){ this.root = new Node(); }
  insert(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub++; for(const ch of w){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) cur.next.set(ch,new Node()); cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub++; } cur.end++; }
  delete(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub--; for(const ch of w){ cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub--; } cur.end--; }
  countPrefix(p){ let cur=this.root; for(const ch of p){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) return 0; cur=cur.next.get(ch); } return cur.sub; }
  kthWord(k){ let res=''; let node=this.root; while(true){ if(k <= node.end) return res; k -= node.end; // skip words ending here
      // iterate in lexical order
      const keys = Array.from(node.next.keys()).sort();
      for(const ch of keys){ const child=node.next.get(ch); if(child.sub >= k){ res += ch; node = child; break; } else k -= child.sub; }
    }
  }
}
```

